.²1 (As a prefix to verbs it means)
.³({%a%}) Away, away from, denoting {#viyoga#}; {#apayAti, apanayati#};
.³({%b%}) deterioration ({#vikfti#}); {#apakaroti#} does wrongly or badly;
.³({%c%}) opposition, negation, contradiction ({#viparIta#}); {#apakarzati, apacinoti#};
.³({%d%}) direction or mention or illustration ({#nidarSana#}); {#apadiSati#};
.³({%e%}) exclusion ({#varjana#}); {#apavah, apasf#} {%<ab>Caus.</ab>%}; ({%f%})
 joy, merriment or laughter ({#Ananda#}); {#apahasati#};
.³({%g%}) concealment or denial ({#cOrya#}); {#apalapati, apavadate#}.
.²2 As first member of <ab>Tat.</ab> or Bahuvrīhi <ab>comp.</ab> it has all the above senses;
 {#apayAnam, apakarma, apapAWaH#}; {#apaSabdaH#} a bad or corrupt word; {#˚BI#}
 fearless; {#˚kalmaza#} stainless; {#aparAgaH#} discontent (<ab>opp.</ab> to {#anurAga#});
 {#˚meGodayaM varzam#} <ls>Ku. 6. 54</ls> <ab>&c.</ab> In most cases {#apa#} may be translated
 by ‘bad’, ‘inferior’, ‘corrupt’, ‘wrong’, ‘unworthy’ <ab>&c.</ab> It also means
 ‘going downwards’ as in {#apAnaH#}.
.²3 As a separable preposition (with a noun in the <ab>abl.</ab>)
.³({%a%}) away from; {#yatsaMpratyapa lokeByo laNkAyAM vasatirBayAt#} <ls>Rām.</ls>;
